			<div class="content" id="post-content-3669290">
									

<p>I understand the appeal of doing the research on Llao yourself, but there are a couple reasons why I don't want to have it be like that:</p>
<ul>
<li>It just feels lazy for me to have the explanation in the SCP, but then basically say &quot;You want to know more? Google an obscure mythological figure you've never heard of before!&quot;</li>
<li>There are two myths about Llao, both of which involve Llao being dead at the bottom of Crater Lake. However, the one in the SCP is the SCP is based on, and the other doesn't work with the SCP.</li>
<li>The myth in the SCP isn't 100% the original myth, and has been tweaked slightly to fit the SCP better.</li>
</ul>
<p>That said, I'll tweak the myth so it's less <em>exactly</em> the SCP, and likely remove some of the changes that I made to make it fit better. (EDIT: I've removed the mention of the pillar from the myth, as well as the monsters plotting to get the heart back.)</p>
<p>It's also worth noting that the Office of Tactical Theology is from spikebrennan's proposal.</p>

