			<div class="content" id="post-content-3674130">
									

<p>Everything that the Foundation/ASCI has done here has only served to make everything worse.</p>
<p>There's the immediate repercussions of the Foundation, which serve to trigger the initial set of four activation events. These clearly and obviously upset the balance between the gods, and allow Llao to possibly become free.</p>
<p>There's also more subtle repercussions, which is that the balance can now be upset while the 3310 remains within Crater Lake (seen in the last three activation events) and that bad stuff is occuring around Crater Lake even while the Old Man is fine (seen in the final log). Both of these are resultant from the removal of SCP-3310 from the lake.</p>
<p>Perhaps I should revise the article to make this clearer, but the Foundation's interferance absolutely resulted in a disruption of the anomaly here. (Or make the Heimal reclassification happen later, because I realize that it wouldn't be Heimal in 1945, when the reclassification occurs.)</p>
<p>I've removed the definition for the time being, in any case.</p>
<p><strong>EDIT:</strong> Nevermind any of this discussion, it's not Hiemal anymore. Archon fits better.</p>

